  ('4aaebb2f-12fd-5b2c-8455-fdb2007ae9f8', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'credentials', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 9, 9, '9', 90, null, null, false, null),
  ('2404885e-7f61-5dee-8ccf-c24d0add31f3', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'SGMs should seek operational assignments as a Senior Manager within a Regional Cyber Center or major command.', '3252c6be586ded1280b498ec3c9b64bcc9fa90c325b08394982736e8dd52b1d1', 9, 9, '9', 91, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5abca15-ce27-5261-8986-d9a93acc63b3', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Self-development', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'DLC 5 is required before attendance to the Sergeants Major Academy. Additionally, SGMs should visit the Army IgnitED website (https://www.armyignited.com) for civilian credentialing associated with their respective MOS. Civilian certifications within IAM and CND roles are required for technical proficiency. SGMs should complete a bachelor’s degree while working towards a master’s degree or higher-level degree plan.', '4fa4e92060e127ca9818a02d91ca96b6f5bdcf063a1f9311fbce9bbb54fff807', 9, 9, '9', 92, null, null, false, null),
  ('afcca822-f0b0-5880-b786-9ca7bcba909d', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Additional training', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'IAM Level III and cybersecurity certification courses.', '6f52c3de03ab61871df4a789fbba408cbafb3e36efa8c2a522e9e85cf81889dd', 9, 9, '9', 93, null, null, false, null),
  ('a28951cb-ba6d-5bdf-8ed4-5b24e1e23c20', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Special assignments', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 9, 9, '9', 94, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5c0974c-8225-5ab1-8f34-00e7d4cf5104', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'See TADECIDE (https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE).', '1cf683b43a39f5162c0adca54fcd998adcad128a29c1f2fdbe6b809ef4701023', 9, 9, '9', 95, null, null, false, null),
  ('0cb10bda-30e4-57b5-953e-cea83ca37457', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25D', null, 'credentials', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 7. Military Occupational Specialty 25D Cyber Network Defender', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 9, 9, '9', 96, null, null, false, null),
  ('611cb944-cfc6-58c6-9bcc-47fea77ef4e9', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'The purpose of the Career Progression Plan is to inform signal Soldiers of the Signal Corps’ intent for their career pattern and PD. To develop spectrum managers to their full potential as professional NCOs, their assignments must follow a pattern of continuous, successive spectrum management positions with increased levels of responsibility. Junior EMSO NCOs should take steps to increase their technical attributes. Soldiers must use online training resources to increase their technical knowledge, and to continue to develop and enhance the skills needed to support the modular force. Follow-on assignments as instructors or Army staff advisors will add to their overall professional knowledge. Spectrum managers are technical experts who are members of the staff at the echelons where they are assigned and do not compete with other MOSs for promotion consideration. MOS 25E has no authorizations for traditional troop leadership positions; there are no Team Chief, Platoon Sergeant, First Sergeant or Command Sergeant Major positions associated with this MOS. MOS 25E Soldiers are not authorized for assignment as a Recruiter, Drill Sergeant, Inspector General or EOA. Soldiers should diversify their careers by requesting non-tactical assignments, as most of the authorizations are in tactical assignments. It is possible that repetitive assignments will occur to meet the needs of the Army. NCOs should communicate their desire for assignments that allow them to remain competitive. Senior NCOs should round out their career with Army level experience.', 'ed438e7106a0f6f9942dd3ed18cf0cda89adbb0ed08d1cb7508d057a8f3bf550', 10, 10, '10', 97, null, null, false, null),
  ('a2f9878e-a5ad-5c9f-aefd-a56769f3e1f5', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'During this phase of their career, Soldiers should focus on continued development and refinement of their technical expertise. Available duty assignments that will increase their experience include BCT, Corps Signal Operations Cells and the OPS section of signal organizations.', 'b87d23c5399945d0b451398e34c1d2125d92249a1d3029efddd7b22f2447f2d1', 10, 10, '10', 98, null, null, false, null),
  ('e7c6a782-f95b-580d-af1e-c3e04f0d382c', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'DLC 3 completion is a prerequisite of attending SLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SSGs for SLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Staff Sergeants who have completed all SLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 4. NCOs should actively seek opportunities to further their civilian and military education. Pursuing a college education, from a degree producing institution, is not a mandatory requirement but one that will place you above your peers. Additional information regarding different degrees and school can be found on the DoD’s TADECIDE website.', '7c837981fc0f7b4ce53f563ebc43125f7d94b496e901037a2cf573c9f8816074', 10, 10, '10', 99, null, null, false, null),
  ('0a1b8b9b-f090-5aae-a88f-af9efdbba193', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'BSNCOC, Space 100 Course. Suggested Army correspondence courses: Principles of Radio Wave Propagation. The Information Technology End-User Curricula in the Army eLearning SmartForce computer-based training may be very useful to EMSO NCO.', 'c59d14029f1d4da5a034703fbde4bce4c5a35a688f3557a03925efee9dd9d231', 10, 10, '10', 100, null, null, false, null),
  ('ba3fbceb-4a8c-5fca-859f-26170a71eecb', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Spectrum Management Assignments: Joint Task Force and Joint Forces Land Component Commands (JTF/JFLCC), Theater and Corps Commands, Instructor/Writer.', '7fb127bab99ce97c79bab7757a62261fe020772ff39bd0e857c0efc354f718ef', 10, 10, '10', 101, null, null, false, null),
  ('b902f7c2-71bd-58a1-8d83-348fcb227a0c', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 10, 10, '10', 102, null, null, false, null),
  ('b77d54fe-9e28-514a-bd84-bd3a16a42377', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'credentials', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 10, 10, '10', 103, null, null, false, null),
  ('daf8ed0a-35cd-522a-b02f-254525e0df9a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — overview', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Operational assignments. During this phase of a career, focus on assignments within Division, Corps, or ASCC staffs. Additional assignments include Instructor, Combined/Joint Commands, and EW cells at Division and Corps.', '50072f4a802c4fe06faedc3792cde126d1bd3d58d328ff2992103d5b74bb6613', 10, 11, '10', 104, null, null, false, null),
  ('e20453c1-9255-5255-897d-6b85ef5f097d', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'DLC 4 completion is a prerequisite of attending SLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SFCs for MLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Sergeants First Class who have completed all SLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 5. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limits the opportunity for civilian education. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion, but it may be a significant factor and should be pursued whenever possible. SFCs should complete an associate degree prior to eligibility for the Master Sergeant Evaluation Board', '8bf6751a6b4b7509c1ae318998a8df5884a568578b0234cb179a1e0b9c6983b9', 11, 11, '11', 105, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd012e80-7830-505f-b9f2-ebb4e72ef75e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Airborne, Air Assault, Space 100, BSNCOC.', 'f7ca57d9b44cc639a649366d826979486946669edbb58062c18f1ca46cfcdc66', 11, 11, '11', 106, null, null, false, null),
  ('e0b8ea3a-0e8c-53a0-9e3e-c7ecf93777b1', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Spectrum Management Assignments: Joint (JTF/JFLCC), Theater and Corps Commands, Instructor/Writer, Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB).', 'f9cf25f1753867e08da5f988876c7b56da0ee78000be6c7e2021fc022a1a40ec', 11, 11, '11', 107, null, null, false, null),
  ('5d4b36b7-1494-5008-8e04-e8fd0441f9ed', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 11, 11, '11', 108, null, null, false, null),
  ('50e27198-4fa2-52f3-a1de-435b87da89e2', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'credentials', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 11, 11, '11', 109, null, null, false, null),
  ('16948fe8-2719-5f54-bbc2-a7b56645d59f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'During this phase of a career, focus on assignments as Division or Corps Spectrum Chief, or on ASCC staffs.', 'e499f3069dbf10745e9de9eec6221f150c878cd0a8fe8f14963b35ac00d48121', 11, 11, '11', 110, null, null, false, null),
  ('e366bbe1-7ef7-5dd4-b7ee-7eae36b0cfbe', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'DLC 5 completion is a prerequisite of attending Sergeants Major Academy. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules MSGs for SMA attendance based on Order of Merit. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion, but it may be a significant factor for selection to SGM and should be pursued whenever possible. Master Sergeants should strive to complete a bachelor’s degree prior to eligibility for the Master Sergeant Evaluation Board.', '1b8475a54511b6610b5e4394f01b42eaa327ad62a4535a43d61e344691c0da4c', 11, 11, '11', 111, null, null, false, null),
  ('a4c4c16a-af3c-5255-87e5-a2f8b9904e76', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'BSNCOC. Suggested correspondence course: None.', 'e500cf9904dda2d6428d3f01484069fc55a569d23d37779761fecc32dbb01281', 11, 11, '11', 112, null, null, false, null),
  ('aacb57ef-1ef9-5dfb-8f0f-17aca02ed27b', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'SFAB.', '886792dbc534835488ee36356f1aed9dbecf0645c6f96da4402122a771d7fd6f', 11, 11, '11', 113, null, null, false, null),
  ('38b3e8b7-2684-52f6-abc9-fb050c6d6caf', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 11, 11, '11', 114, null, null, false, null),
  ('f9b9cd1c-e489-57ea-8421-27a4ba3da3bf', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'credentials', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 11, 11, '11', 115, null, null, false, null),
  ('33eec11b-dcac-55a6-af94-6ce9ca1f6a7d', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Forces Command (FORSCOM), CIO–G6, ASCC Army Spectrum Chief (named or numbered Army echelon command, such as the Third Army or HQ U.S. Army Pacific Command).', 'f9f6096ea9fc91f8eb248cb4070332e5e6b3a031ca0c10cc8012f7ff0af50832', 11, 11, '11', 116, null, null, false, null),
  ('2165fc08-5f1e-5f7c-86a9-506474648645', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Self-development', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Under DLC, SGMs are automatically enrolled in DLC 5 upon completion of the SGM-A. DLC 5 tasks are primarily focused at nominative and Joint Staff levels. SGMs should have a bachelor’s degree and should continue in courses to obtain a master’s degree.', '377bced68a3fe93d023d2830f5515d51b9a688465dc96024c9e3c31eb00133bb', 11, 11, '11', 117, null, null, false, null),
  ('3dfacbd2-e9fa-5858-8812-e1f0e2e49f3c', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Additional training', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 11, 11, '11', 118, null, null, false, null),
  ('0606d82d-dadf-5466-9b83-cc8fedbbbba7', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Suggested correspondence course', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 11, 11, '11', 119, null, null, false, null),
  ('59c78f38-4d17-5bb9-a48c-0a5326d4421a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Special assignments', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 11, 11, '11', 120, null, null, false, null),
  ('0d85826e-fde3-5d00-b033-f3425e6dada3', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 11, 11, '11', 121, null, null, false, null),
  ('01d18b34-5b69-51e4-bde8-c26edb69caae', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25E', null, 'credentials', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 10. Military Occupational Specialty 25E Electromagnetic Spectrum Manager', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 11, 11, '11', 122, null, null, false, null),
  ('08ff9c9b-b886-5320-b879-fa2982c153bb', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'The purpose of the Career Progression Plan is to inform Soldiers the Signal Corps’ intent for their career pattern and PD. Junior enlisted Soldiers should take steps to increase their technical and basic soldiering attributes. Soldiers should use online training resources to increase their knowledge of complex Internet Protocol (IP) based systems and equipment that is needed to support the modular force. Junior enlisted assignments must focus on challenging and demanding jobs such as Team Chief and Section Chief. Soldiers should avoid repetitive assignments outside of the MOS (such as consecutive Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor/Writer, staff, or similar duty assignments) whenever possible. This will ensure necessary diversity throughout the career path. It is possible repetitive assignments will occur to meet the needs of the Army. Soldiers should communicate their desire for assignments that allow them to remain competitive.', '07502089574670d0bdf91096989b8b3e55cf8a8cc1ccc6936f81cc77ec1c013b', 12, 12, '12', 123, null, null, false, null),
  ('d2a564ff-4f27-54b9-a60c-11ce073d407f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Advanced Individual Training (AIT); Basic Leader Course (BLC) for SPC/CPL.', '3f1a01d13a943b19ba07fe80bcbeece28469654ff6c1d9bb599db92de504f7b0', 12, 12, '12', 124, null, null, false, null),
  ('3f86a10c-28bd-52d8-8294-fed09c3be2c2', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'A Soldier should focus on building a strong base of technical expertise, basic MOS skills, and common Soldier tasks during the early years of their career. Assignments such as Network Communication Systems Specialist, Transmission Systems Operator, Cable Systems Installer, TROPO Systems Operator, or Range Extension Operator. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display leadership skills, initiative, and motivation.', 'b44cdf944bea15f1a120ef0222e34bba7f4ee189dc7029186088ffba5a8fb575', 12, 12, '12', 125, null, null, false, null),
  ('ed4ee39a-d199-58ae-ae8c-d7f12e5c8e73', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Under DLC 1, Soldiers must be a graduate of Initial Military Training (IMT) and have been promoted to SPC. Soldiers in the rank of PVT through SPC will not be enrolled into DLC 1 until promoted to SPC. Soldiers entering the Army as SPC must have 18 months’ time in service (TIS) prior to enrollment into DLC 1. Under guided self-development, Soldiers and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes the Internet and Army correspondence courses, CLEP and DANTES. Soldiers may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. The completion of a college level English course is recommended prior to attending the BLC. Soldiers should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. Soldiers may enroll in the Army Correspondence Course Program online through Army Training Requirements and Resources System (ATRRS), and/or Joint Knowledge Online (JKO).', 'ce25664473dfce7d4478f96cf16579ab69fd738d711d68b7cc873086a4a4b040', 12, 13, '12', 126, null, null, false, null),
  ('2428af4f-0914-50ea-9208-8daaba7c0982', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Basic Airborne Corse and Air Assault Course. Suggested Army correspondence courses: Network Switching Systems Operator-Maintainer Course, Multichannel Transmission Systems Operator Maintainer Course, Antenna Installation Course, and Cable Splicing Course. There is also an online Joint Network Node (JNN) simulation that is available via the Fort Eisenhower eLandWarNet University.', '498f4507bb2648427f48f5f7e1e2d4813705a47a02475ff8733a92a7b8df9c88', 13, 13, '13', 127, null, null, false, null),
  ('b07f99f6-8902-5c15-9808-55c992343bd2', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'WHCA.', 'a87fbf69a5404b6236849ee86d6304721da3a556979025ba3fd6958c8b5396a0', 13, 13, '13', 128, null, null, false, null),
  ('ae6a1cd3-fcfe-5f36-b88e-7b4bad14d662', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 13, 13, '13', 129, null, null, false, null),
  ('5908fbe7-f23e-5461-a530-02475dca1876', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'credentials', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com. Suggested credentials IAT level I.', '86ef5ecbfdf92a36803ef7696215c936b2dac8d90b01db59c49d7fbc8fcf0ce2', 13, 13, '13', 130, null, null, false, null),
  ('f4900b1c-f35d-536b-abc0-e565370c68e1', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Advanced Leader Course (ALC). Successful graduation with honors from this course could be a significant promotion factor.', 'bc5f864e42f54efb86118daa5184c6b6122f167438464913651d1cd621ae29ec', 13, 13, '13', 131, null, null, false, null),
  ('3f0d420e-a32b-542a-bd9e-b6c079c18865', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'During this phase of a career, NCOs should focus on tactical assignments to develop Soldier leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge. NCOs at every opportunity should seek the positions that allow them to gain leadership experience such as Sr Network Communication Systems Specialist, Sr Transmissions Systems Operator, Sr Cable Systems Installer, or Sr TROPO Systems Operator.', 'ecd5e8a75ca59162311499a4b46189e6b8674987f0913dd3bfe84f45a731dad1', 13, 13, '13', 132, null, null, false, null),
  ('ded6bdd3-8d31-5535-af9e-161180f53aaf', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'DLC 2 completion is a prerequisite of attending ALC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SGTs for ALC attendance based on Order of Merit. Sergeants who have completed all ALC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 3. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes online college courses, Army correspondence courses, CLEP, and DANTES. Soldiers may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. Soldiers should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. Soldiers may enroll in the Army Correspondence Course Program online through Army Training Requirements and Resources System (ATRRS), and/or Joint Knowledge Online (JKO).', '17b5a1090873b40d30722cf5fd923d9d71fca04d8220aa13d74ca854fa523819', 13, 13, '13', 133, null, null, false, null),
  ('0d83b272-0f23-5de6-a0c9-56e7eb391ed2', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Basic Airborne Corse, Air Assault Course, COMSEC Account Manager Course, Jumpmaster Course, Marksmanship Master Trainer Course, Master Resilience Trainer. There is an online JNN simulation that is available via the Fort Eisenhower LandWarNet University.', 'f553353fa4b88ea4f9b8717e8be40b5e49286ef9b958609d9ac32e6875c19320', 13, 13, '13', 134, null, null, false, null),
  ('fa77c27c-014e-5d74-a307-48b9fa9f949f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'WHCA, Instructor/Writer, Training Development, Joint Communication Support Element, Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB), and Joint Communication Unit.', '2ec950599713d268de813c68deeee2fffe0684119d5f8a51684aa99cba64df11', 13, 13, '13', 135, null, null, false, null),
  ('d1c44c0d-15de-55e9-a97a-8d8f8a2549f0', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE', '5db5cbbe6f980b489a8041ba94a06711ad49a1bc8b2aaf832dee11f89f5acc15', 13, 13, '13', 136, null, null, false, null),
  ('e71ddcc2-7ea5-5750-92b3-a8c14d96631a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'credentials', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com. Suggested credentials IAT level I and IAT level II.', '157044ecfe7740257d0f33f34aa8894f4354a3e7b22c5ff5bebac7350247f920', 13, 13, '13', 137, null, null, false, null),
  ('6477090a-4c84-52c8-b9d6-cc40933d5b06', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Senior Leader Course (SLC); Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC). Successful graduation with honors from these courses may be a significant promotion factor.', 'a720e6d1b8e8dec848bb443b70f59c2da29dc8d544c22fd4009a251d0bf1453e', 13, 13, '13', 138, null, null, false, null),
  ('d74cde5a-6ce6-554d-8b2b-41a8a3e5e1d3', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'NCOs should focus on continued development and refinement of their skills with assignments, which develop leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge during this phase of their career. NCOs at every opportunity should seek positions to gain leadership experience such as Network Communication Systems Supervisor, Cable Systems Installer Supervisor, Transmissions System Team Supervisor, Section Supervisor, Network Communications Transmissions Systems Supervisor, and Plans/Operations NCO.', '5483455668a4620179f74be4cb67ac2ff5b850daed11aab0fefb4ad76094f43e', 13, 14, '13', 139, null, null, false, null),
  ('953df18f-e5c6-5ce3-9533-672a99c02623', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'DLC 3 completion is a prerequisite of attending SLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SSGs for SLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Staff Sergeants who have completed all SLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 4. NCOs should actively seek opportunities to further their civilian and military education. Pursuing a college education, from a degree producing institution, is not a mandatory requirement but one that will place you above your peers.', '4f61d843a35add5d61be6ac74b349ba53ffb73f8f50bdb296becd133194134c1', 14, 14, '14', 140, null, null, false, null),
  ('633a7021-5229-5d7c-b6c9-f20a79edbb91', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault, and Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC), COMSEC Account Manager Course, Jumpmaster Course, Marksmanship Master Trainer Course, Master Resilience Trainer, Master Fitness Training Course, SHARP Foundation Course. Suggested Army correspondence courses: Network Switching Systems Operator-Maintainer Course. There is an online JNN simulation that is available via the Fort Eisenhower LandWarNet University.', '9a6478f748a686f3507759805e12dee55ed3e76dbe9584d2e9aa57094271d418', 14, 14, '14', 141, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad72f776-9ed3-55d4-a3b2-9ae883a84f1b', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Instructor/Writer, Drill Sergeant, Detailed Recruiter, Small Group Leader (SGL), Training Development, AC/RC Advisor, Observer/Controller, NATO, SFAB, and WHCA.', '9dfd3a425040766fa505550817989f45ffabca10606d87b8095a8693b6fafda7', 14, 14, '14', 142, null, null, false, null),
  ('89d32c03-7d12-509a-88bf-10b6a02be417', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE', '5db5cbbe6f980b489a8041ba94a06711ad49a1bc8b2aaf832dee11f89f5acc15', 14, 14, '14', 143, null, null, false, null),
  ('934f1c18-bb59-5c9f-8bc1-a592d84a4d02', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'credentials', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com. Suggested IAT level I and IAT level II.', '00ea01d6b20c80481e4b17571517f77ceea09b6ef09abf6986af504506610e5d', 14, 14, '14', 144, null, null, false, null),
  ('0acdd7af-8e7b-5527-a5e2-ec05d9179c12', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Master Leader Course (MLC). Successful graduation with honors from this course may be a significant promotion factor.', '6d959374d315d399472678204aa6afef406e8cf6a68d858ababb975f643fad4a', 14, 14, '14', 145, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e9d39c9-d78f-5b45-b779-94a6a045936b', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'SFCs should seek assignments as a Platoon Sergeant, Detachment Sergeants, Network Communication Systems Manager, Network Communication Systems Planner, and Switch Systems Chief.', '899a34798c0569e68d38cc3a12d7213b8d35d608c9dbc1f3366845b5b95de0b7', 14, 14, '14', 146, null, null, false, null),
  ('ce9882d2-9e23-5201-ae4b-160b569b57a1', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Under DLC, Sergeants First Class are enrolled automatically in DLC 4 upon completion of SLC. It is highly recommended that DLC 4 be completed prior to assuming duties as a First Sergeant. DLC 4 completion is required for consideration for promotion to Master Sergeant. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion, but it may be a significant factor and should be pursued whenever possible. A SFC should strive to complete an associate degree prior to eligibility for the Sergeant First Class Evaluation Board. NCOs should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. Upon selection for promotion to Master Sergeant, Sergeants First Class must attend Master Leader Course to be promoted under the Select, Train, Educate, and Promote (STEP) program. There is no DLC requirement for promotion due to the requirement for DLC 4 completion to be eligible for selection to Master Sergeant.', 'a4c4d41cc5fffd0599233a5703f70739ad1ac9fa49b8e09361753e6d613c31b8', 14, 14, '14', 147, null, null, false, null),
  ('aa7ad6e8-5511-5a35-acd7-181552fdb885', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC), Mission Command Digital Master Gunner Course (MCDMG-C), Signal Digital Master Gunner Course (SDMG-C), Common Faculty Development-Instructor Course (CFD-IC), Joint C4 Planners Course Operational Contract Support Course (OCS), Equal Opportunity Advisor Course (EOAC), SHARP, Master Resiliency Trainer Course (MRTC), Master Fitness Trainer Course (MFTC), Management Client Course (MGC), Ranger School, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, and Company Commander/First Sergeant Course. Suggested correspondence courses: None.', '77658f0b4d4884aa7127b60a6f442934989338376a171cdbe39c4d0b9119ba3d', 14, 15, '14', 148, null, null, false, null),
  ('f66fa676-c16c-59c9-bc1c-d142f30b2592', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Senior Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Career Management NCO, Career Advisor (HRC), Instructor/Writer, Training Developer, Senior Small Group Leader, Observer Controller/Trainer, Inspector General, Equal Opportunity Advisor, Special Missions Unit, White House Communications Agency, Defense Information Systems Agency, Joint Communications Support Element, Joint Communications Unit, Security Forces Assistance Brigade, Defense Attaché.', 'bda22918351c3b8e476d0351d452d43b87c2640cb60804939c262850dbe07d10', 15, 15, '15', 149, null, null, false, null),
  ('f4805b5b-204b-5c82-8887-8d315c12e2da', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 15, 15, '15', 150, null, null, false, null),
  ('63a7ebf5-9273-50bf-8247-032031e735ce', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25H', null, 'credentials', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 13. Military Occupational Specialty 25H Network Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com. Suggested certifications: Information Assurance Technician Level II-III, Information Assurance Manager Level I-II.', 'f6ce17c4266ee2866e00f623542fabfed20d7faf50442177678e0e12e05d8c51', 15, 15, '15', 151, null, null, false, null),
  ('63e6f9b3-e5c0-5081-a060-2e84e0d7bcbf', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'The purpose of the Career Progression Plan is to inform Soldiers the Signal Corps’ intent for their career pattern and PD. Junior enlisted Soldiers should take steps to increase their technical and basic Soldiering attributes. Junior NCO assignments must focus on challenging and demanding roles such as Team Chief and Section Chief. SNCOs should seek positions such as Platoon Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, First Sergeant, or other leadership positions and serve in special and joint assignments. Follow-on assignments at the brigade and division staff will add to their overall professional knowledge and diversity. Soldiers should avoid repetitive assignments outside of MOS (such as going from Drill Sergeant to Recruiter duty, Instructor, staff, or similar positions) at every opportunity. It is possible that repetitive assignments will occur to meet the needs of the Army. Soldiers should interject and communicate their desire for assignments that allow them to remain competitive. SNCOs should round out their career with battalion, brigade or higher-level experience.', '99f103ff954edb80e2fe6127b4aabe458222c93ba7502030f738a36ccdb5cd34', 15, 16, '15', 152, null, null, false, null),
  ('37a3b1d9-914f-5d52-b30b-d29501965c7e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'The MOS 25S course establishes the responsibilities of the satellite communication systems specialist for supervising, installing, operating, and maintaining strategic and tactical satellite communications systems. When the Soldier is later assigned to another unit with different equipment sets, they will have a core basis of knowledge, which should be enhanced with additional on-the-job training.', 'c6a0b0e263fd1b3094516a44a1511eee3b3623c11a64bd0494a212c02525ee76', 16, 16, '16', 153, null, null, false, null),
  ('4dac8402-5040-5dfa-ab58-54756c1fdcbe', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Soldiers must focus on building a strong base of technical expertise on equipment, MOS skills, and common Soldier tasks during the early years of their career. Where possible, Soldiers should build a base of knowledge obtained in both strategic and tactical units. Assignments such as SATCOM Systems Specialist, Military Strategic and Tactical Relay (MILSTAR) Terminal Operator-Maintainer, Long Haul Operator- Maintainer, and Circuit Controller enhance technical and operational expertise. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills, initiative, and motivation. Self-development. Under DLC 1, Soldiers must be a graduate of Initial Military Training (IMT) and have been promoted to SPC. Soldiers in the rank of E-1 through E-3 will not be enrolled into DLC 1 until promoted to SPC. Soldiers entering the Army as SPC must have 18 months of time in service (TIS) prior to enrollment into DLC 1. Under guided self-development, Soldiers and their chain of command must exploit every educational opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes the Internet and Army correspondence courses, CLEP and DANTES. Soldiers may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. The completion of a college level English course is recommended prior to attending the BLC. Soldiers should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. Soldiers may enroll in the Army Correspondence Course Program online through Army Training Requirements and Resources System (ATRRS), and/or Joint Knowledge Online (JKO).', '2822ce0a1e0044b3d51805ecb39c7dad8f8c3a90236fa903d22c1b101f6342ff', 16, 16, '16', 154, null, null, false, null),
  ('2dd8ccad-4f9f-54b3-b393-fdfa2bc1ed85', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Additional training WHCA Console Control Operations, Ranger, Airborne, and Air Assault. Suggested Army correspondence courses: None.', '705ce43fda66c8254514d684919a2d95bde674140b67cca86bc6df78d48f440a', 16, 16, '16', 155, null, null, false, null),
  ('8c6051f0-185a-5fc6-9a03-848a4ad91a45', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Security Force Assistance Brigades (SFAB).', '149bf2ab95684a8b27018b52ef1ae252ffc23011f51dd34bcc7d7b94780403a2', 16, 16, '16', 156, null, null, false, null),
  ('dcc8520b-899b-55a9-a9b2-66756671b16b', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 16, 16, '16', 157, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec2109f6-f675-5ea2-80bc-9bdaa1eaab8f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'credentials', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 16, 16, '16', 158, null, null, false, null),
  ('bdd9a796-3f31-5ec9-95ec-141274b84a61', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Advanced Leader Course (ALC); Master Resilience Course (MRT). Successful graduation with honors from this course could be a significant promotion factor.', '56bdaa0333161e19008fc8e68a7449dc71b1b09b0108b0493c4de4db70b10cdc', 16, 16, '16', 159, null, null, false, null),
  ('d192627f-d653-5bf8-b13f-581a8da85554', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'During this phase of a career, NCOs should focus on assignments that enable development of Soldier leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge. NCOs should seek positions to gain leadership experience such as Circuit Control Team Chief, Senior SATCOM Systems Specialist, MILSTAR Senior Operator, SATCOM Operations Sergeant, SATCOM Maintenance NCO, and Circuit Management NCO at every opportunity.', 'e4cf1f1406cbc4192b81ca2ec6917726d882b1912e73a712b817ecead042cdf5', 16, 16, '16', 160, null, null, false, null),
  ('bbe7cf01-10a7-5132-8fcb-f0ef4866d77e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'DLC 2 completion is a prerequisite of attending ALC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SGTs for ALC attendance based on Order of Merit. Sergeants who have completed all ALC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 3. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every educational opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes taking Online Courses through an accredited college or university, Army correspondence courses, CLEP, and DANTES. Sergeants may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Sergeants should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. The completion of a college level English course is recommended prior to attending the BLC. Sergeants should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. Soldiers may enroll in the Army Correspondence Course Program online through Army Training Requirements and Resources System (ATRRS), and/or Joint Knowledge Online (JKO).', 'bfc9cbc7cf9ce20f68f91adee55b1f1056751ac61ff1b026f3a5d229ae609334', 16, 17, '16', 161, null, null, false, null),
  ('5b43b68d-e9e0-5306-bed3-1c05d1671d62', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Ranger, Airborne, Air Assault, the Jumpmaster Course, and Common Faculty Development-Instructor Course, Marksmanship Master Trainer Course, COMSEC Account Manager Course, Advanced EHF Mission Planner Course.', 'c27e3f8a8054f3b8dde12853882de9fef29cdc7d1e8a8fbfab7bd4eea3ae8d79', 17, 17, '17', 162, null, null, false, null),
  ('61ebcf2e-e1c6-5513-8047-dce0fbfcedec', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Suggested Army correspondence courses', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (SEJPME) 1 Course.', '834291db6a32e72c055fceb03e24239b1b41cff4d7841df612371234126870b4', 17, 17, '17', 163, null, null, false, null),
  ('441fbeac-efdd-5c28-a073-13fa51a37b51', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Security Force Assistance Brigades (SFABs), Joint Communications Support Element (JCSE).', '4545f2ff75360f4bef84c04e1dab8e3be55212d3e99d258f873375a4ab896e20', 17, 17, '17', 164, null, null, false, null),
  ('2cd4fa6b-f5cb-5e67-9df2-6fe158219082', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 17, 17, '17', 165, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e801510-8783-54df-81b6-782863f8ae7f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'credentials', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 17, 17, '17', 166, null, null, false, null),
  ('b73338dc-18ba-5005-8da8-702b3f12323f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Senior Leader Course (SLC); Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC). Successful graduation with honors from these courses may be a significant promotion factor.', 'a720e6d1b8e8dec848bb443b70f59c2da29dc8d544c22fd4009a251d0bf1453e', 17, 17, '17', 167, null, null, false, null),
  ('0d0252a6-92da-5bb1-9199-d694c0f35369', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'NCOs should focus on continued development and refinement of their skills with assignments that develop leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge during this phase of their career. NCOs should seek positions to gain leadership experience such as SATCOM System Supervisor, Circuit Control Supervisor, MILSTAR Team Chief,Senior Circuit Management NCO, SATCOM Maintenance Supervisor, and SATCOM Operations NCO at every opportunity. Likewise, NCOs should seek positions that broaden the force such as Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, Developer, or ALC Small Group Leader (SGL) while avoiding consecutive assignments outside of their MOS.', 'e539e84468baf7fc3cd1e18a8d46db01fa57c94e71312572a8a8f03ac832fe44', 17, 17, '17', 168, null, null, false, null),
  ('e9ca5134-4e62-5ce4-b93d-15177191a6d8', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'DLC 3 completion is a prerequisite of attending SLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SSGs for SLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Staff Sergeants who have completed all SLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 4. NCOs should actively seek opportunities to further their civilian and military education. Pursuing a college education from a degree producing institution is not a mandatory requirement but may offer favorable results during NCO Evaluation Boards. NCOs should plan their college program around a degree that relates to their MOS using information provided on the TADECIDE website.', '5058695b896af47e4685d382f94923eb35e4cb5ecc342007a0032f8e5c879b9d', 17, 17, '17', 169, null, null, false, null),
  ('d029c457-8cce-58a9-8552-500cd6bbe32e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Airborne, Air Assault, Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Common Faculty Development-Instructor Course, BSNCOC, Master Resilience Course (MRT), Equal Opportunities Leaders Course (EOLC), SHARP Foundation Course and the Jumpmaster Course, Master Fitness Trainer Course, Marksmanship Master Trainer Course, Joint C4 Planner Course, Advanced EHF Mission Planner Course.', 'cebba3f308bfac96aaf583d2f8ff5af94b35d698970a289ec0dde8d4374823d4', 17, 17, '17', 170, null, null, false, null),
  ('80f7396d-0a07-5686-b442-75f7edc8c712', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Suggested Army correspondence courses', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (SEJPME) 1 Course.', '834291db6a32e72c055fceb03e24239b1b41cff4d7841df612371234126870b4', 17, 17, '17', 171, null, null, false, null),
  ('7a40ceab-9e35-5667-907e-6e581bb47f85', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Drill Sergeant, Platoon Sergeant, WHCA, ALC Small Group Leader, Instructor/Writer, SFAB, and Detailed Recruiter.', 'bbd939a0d3f938ad5acc5b2082fa491e3546f07a48cb4d515e70adcaafed14d1', 17, 17, '17', 172, null, null, false, null),
  ('3a0c834b-1cae-5d11-9c4b-7ccd96766996', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 17, 17, '17', 173, null, null, false, null),
  ('80581bf0-866d-5786-8b64-40814f5d8cd6', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'credentials', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 17, 17, '17', 174, null, null, false, null),
  ('9f2df6fa-d065-54c6-9088-293921a9f936', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Master Leader Course (MLC), Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC) Successful graduation with honors from this course may be a significant promotion factor.', '367a60fd0e4ec1ba05dbeb1d6d36257de558533272aea0997216c48bdc913d52', 18, 18, '18', 175, null, null, false, null),
  ('c91a8f25-f3e8-528a-a18b-e2f62c705f94', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'SFCs should seek assignments as a Platoon Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, Section Chief, SATCOM Terminal Chiefand Senior SATCOM Operations NCO. Likewise, NCOs should seek positions that broaden the force such as Drill Sergeant, Recruiter, Instructor, Developer, or SLC Small Group Leader (SGL) while avoiding consecutive assignments outside of their MOS. Self-development. Under DLC, Sergeants First Class are enrolled automatically in DLC 4 upon completion of SLC. It is highly recommended that DLC 4 be completed prior to assuming duties as a First Sergeant. DLC 4 completion is required for consideration for promotion to Master Sergeant. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every educational opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion, but it may be a significant factor and should be pursued whenever possible. It is recommended that a SFC complete an associate degree prior to eligibility for the Master Sergeant Evaluation Board. Upon selection for promotion to Master Sergeant, Sergeants First Class must attend the Master Leader Course under the Select, Train, Educate, and Promote (STEP) program. There is no DLC requirement for promotion due to the requirement for DLC 4 completion to be eligible for selection to Master Sergeant.', '5467272d304ba1957930e4a2b2b05b0d21334da9fbea9edaa54763ef49dc55fa', 18, 18, '18', 176, null, null, false, null),
  ('e93e103e-e15a-57f9-9186-5c760589496a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Battlefield Spectrum Management, Airborne, Air Assault, Drill Sergeant, Joint C4 Planners Course, SHARP Foundation Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor Course (EOAC), BSNCOC, Advanced EHF Mission Planner Course', '2cf1a64a40a6742f8ebc425ba00b16de48cce47f5d4fb56e9de36cfff5376eb6', 18, 18, '18', 177, null, null, false, null),
  ('0b2a16f4-7e62-5bb4-8069-0f30d8105dfa', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'SLC Small Group Leader, Senior Drill Sergeant, Drill Sergeant, Platoon Sergeant, WHCA, Senior Instructor/Writer, EOA, Career Management NCO, Training with Industry (TWI) and AC/RC Advisor.', '0e7d57fe4d3e967843a04c29b6fada3945fc27475b2758c1a1d0d34251201c08', 18, 18, '18', 178, null, null, false, null),
  ('f182a21a-2208-5e13-897b-af2413a4cafc', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.', '48c53bdd1229a3fe93316b57830807c7d004ade617663baeceb3e9af00723509', 18, 18, '18', 179, null, null, false, null),
  ('ba8ce9be-9338-5e5e-93af-7a966cb23c94', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25S', null, 'credentials', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 16. Military Occupational Specialty 25S Satellite Communication Systems Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com. Suggested Army correspondence courses: Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (SEJPME) 2 Course.', 'b9db7de475804bf9f96032ead489827ea0509040298df512f5d612ba478eb024', 18, 18, '18', 180, null, null, false, null),
  ('2a5fbd0a-5e80-5039-b974-bdff62c6e1bd', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'The purpose of the Career Progression Plan is to inform Soldiers the Signal Corps’ intent for career pattern and PD. Soldiers should steadily increase their technical and basic Soldiering attributes. NCOs should use online training resources to continue to develop and enhance the skills needed to support the modular force. Junior enlisted Soldiers should take steps to increase their technical and basic soldiering attributes. Junior NCO assignments must focus on the hard, demanding jobs such as Team Chief and Section Chief. Senior NCOs should seek positions such as Section Chief, Platoon Sergeant, Signal Operations Section Chief, and First Sergeant. Follow-on assignments, as SNCOs at the brigade and above staff positions, as well as special assignments such as Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Inspector General NCO, and ROTC Military Science Instructor will add to their overall professional knowledge as their career matures. Soldiers assigned to TDA units should seek challenging positions, such as ALC or SLC Small Group Leader (SGLs) and take advantage of opportunities to serve in special or joint assignments. Priority or special assignments such as, Instructor/Writer, Observer/ Controller (OC), Drill Sergeant, Detailed Recruiter, EOA, Career Management NCO (Signal Proponent), Career Advisor (Signal Branch), and Inspector General NCOs are career enhancing. Soldiers should avoid repetitive assignments, outside of MOS whenever possible. This will ensure necessary diversity throughout the career path. It is possible repetitive assignments will occur to meet the needs of the Army. Soldiers should interject and communicate their desire for assignments that allow them to remain competitive. NCOs should round out their career with Army level operations experience. SNCOs should round out their career with battalion, brigade, or higher-level experience.', '89e782f490468058f45012b96cee5d43582a912e6e3831b05d22cd74a3e5cd87', 19, 19, '19', 181, null, null, false, null),
  ('337629c6-e386-5d17-85a4-24c3fc5d9406', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Advanced Individual Training (AIT); Basic Leader Course (BLC) for SPC/CPL.', '3f1a01d13a943b19ba07fe80bcbeece28469654ff6c1d9bb599db92de504f7b0', 19, 19, '19', 182, null, null, false, null),
  ('2353f2d4-f16a-559e-9584-c8f1cccfa1df', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'During the early years of a career, Soldiers should focus on building a strong base of technical expertise, basic MOS skills, and common Soldier tasks. Assignments such as Signal Operations Support Specialist, Radio Retransmission Operator, Forward Signal Support Specialist, and Signal Tactical Network Specialist to enhance technical and operational expertise are recommended. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills, initiative, and motivation.', '07404af2f6d2bc7710e5934f2870684ac503473c6370f23aaa1ca07d8c382107', 19, 19, '19', 183, null, null, false, null),
  ('3850af88-379f-52ff-990e-cc4e6210087e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Under DLC 1, Soldiers must be a graduate of Initial Military Training (IMT) and have been promoted to SPC. Soldiers in the rank of E-1 through E-3 will not be enrolled into DLC 1 until promoted to SPC. Soldiers entering the Army as SPC must have 18 months’ time in service (TIS) prior to enrollment into DLC 1. Under guided self-development, Soldiers and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes the Internet and Army correspondence courses, CLEP and DANTES. Soldiers may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. The completion of a college level English course is recommended prior to attending BLC. Soldiers should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. The Army Distributed Learning Program (TADLP) can be found by visiting https://tadlp.tradoc.army.mil/. Soldiers can register with The Joint Services Transcript (JST) at https://jst.doded.mil/official.html. The JST can convert military training into college credit hours for submission to school towards a degree program.', 'fe59e1d7f89fe6c293add3e838ed21cc0f54c0607c83ce904b59f8002a5cf8e4', 19, 19, '19', 184, null, null, false, null),
  ('4bf69feb-ddcd-5985-850f-83319f336181', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Airborne and Air Assault. Suggested Distance Learning Courses: Basic Leaders Course (SPC/CPL), Signal Operations Support SPC Course, and Signal Leadership Course (SPC–SGT). Suggested certifications: CompTIA A+, Network +, and Security +.', 'b91e82e3cdc050da09c8fc3b9491e79695022a61e4156ac74f4f07773980250f', 19, 20, '19', 185, null, null, false, null),
  ('8ad43936-363f-58ea-96d8-45322d2aeeba', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 20, 20, '20', 186, null, null, false, null),
  ('ccefc270-9bf4-5708-93e3-485153d9050a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE', '5db5cbbe6f980b489a8041ba94a06711ad49a1bc8b2aaf832dee11f89f5acc15', 20, 20, '20', 187, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ba1273c-9e51-5077-8fe6-0d7ad7d0d6f5', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'credentials', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private - Specialist/Corporal — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 20, 20, '20', 188, null, null, false, null),
  ('dfa934b9-3ec9-5079-80a7-f10869cbe5ee', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Advanced Leader Course. Successful graduation with honors from this course could be a significant promotion factor.', 'bbee7ad504a8e023bacdf5d6b3735c1126db547ccad7f65d3fd4e77ee9986556', 20, 20, '20', 189, null, null, false, null),
  ('524c1b6d-5318-5fdf-9ba7-ac1c01a8b061', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'During this phase of a career, NCOs should focus on tactical assignments, to develop Soldier leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge. NCOs should be familiar with DA Pam 611–21 and seek the positions that allow them to gain technical knowledge by serving in the position of Forward Signal Support NCO and leadership experience by serving in the position of Team Chief, Signal Operations NCO, and Signal Maintenance NCO. Self-development. DLC 2 completion is a prerequisite of attending ALC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SGTs for ALC attendance based on Order of Merit. Sergeants who have completed all ALC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 3. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. There are alternative methods for obtaining college credits outside of the traditional classroom instruction. This includes the Internet and Army correspondence courses, CLEP and DANTES. Soldiers may convert military education and experience to college credit by maximizing the TADECIDE program. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. The completion of a college level English course is recommended prior to attending the BLC. Soldiers should use this time to improve their ASVAB scores as appropriate. Soldiers should see their chain of command and the installation education office for more information on education programs and financial support. The Army Distributed Learning Program (TADLP) can be found by visiting https://tadlp.tradoc.army.mil/. Soldiers can register with The Joint Services Transcript (JST) at https://jst.doded.mil/official.html. The JST can be used to convert military training into college credit hours for submission to school towards a degree program.', '16c91895ad4f12fc7c8e4ed823694e538812456fc3ebfe68c0a3e2b14af30076', 20, 20, '20', 190, null, null, false, null),
  ('934b663b-7d93-5bd1-ba50-a25818b614a9', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Airborne and Air Assault. Suggested correspondence courses: None. Suggested technical certificates: CompTIA A+, Network +, and Security +.', '49b272e7a1b623e617c5df2cfd71678dc1ed28ecb8dd9f508063c07d69109f45', 20, 20, '20', 191, null, null, false, null),
  ('497000fd-abe1-5e5d-81d6-3efe05064a9e', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Defense Information Systems Agency (DISA), White House Communications Agency (WHCA), Security Forces Advisory Brigade (SFAB), Joint Communications Unit (JCU) and Training Developer.', '194966963444758d0e2f9334eb26520b43558e2c6c54c7ce707e2a264d97001f', 20, 20, '20', 192, null, null, false, null),
  ('c27d33dd-c6c2-593f-8938-e5dfc769285b', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE', 'b0362e8c2e40e8ac31bf3147d4c9682a79248406b618265bb27c71abab87747b', 20, 20, '20', 193, null, null, false, null),
  ('a4020f87-a30b-5d7b-9f5a-71c658512d1f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'credentials', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 20, 20, '20', 194, null, null, false, null),
  ('b15fa542-8743-55a8-86e3-23ba2ad94b74', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Senior Leader Course (SLC); Battle Staff NCO Course (BSNCOC). Successful graduation with honors from these courses may be a significant promotion factor.', 'a720e6d1b8e8dec848bb443b70f59c2da29dc8d544c22fd4009a251d0bf1453e', 20, 20, '20', 195, null, null, false, null),
  ('1e2020bb-a7b3-5f23-9569-ebb8fb0c6c51', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'NCOs should focus on continued development and refinement of their skills with assignments, which develop leadership skills, hone technical expertise, and lay a foundation of tactical knowledge during this phase of their career. Duty positions such as Signal Operations NCO, Radio Retransmission Supervisor, Forward Signal Support NCO and ALC Small Group Leader will increase experience and intensify leadership skills. NCOs should avoid back-to-back special duty assignments such as Drill Sergeant, Detail Recruiter, or any repetitive combination of assignments whenever possible. This reduces MOS proficiency due to continuous changes in modernization, structure, and doctrine.', '2c4b020bcc608cd2fb35b57984cde1c3e063fdb586e3134913ffcfb5149babb2', 20, 20, '20', 196, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e95c667-8601-56d5-9a25-e954df485539', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'DLC 3 completion is a prerequisite of attending SLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SSGs for SLC attendance based on Order of Merit. Staff Sergeants who have completed all SLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 4. NCOs should actively seek opportunities to further their civilian and military education. Pursuing a college education, from a degree producing institution, is not a mandatory requirement but one that will place you above your peers.', '4f61d843a35add5d61be6ac74b349ba53ffb73f8f50bdb296becd133194134c1', 21, 21, '21', 197, null, null, false, null),
  ('914ffa44-3cbb-56ba-8e9f-122ab60db045', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'EOA, Drill Sergeant, Detailed Recruiter, Airborne, Air Assault, and BSNCOC. Suggested correspondence courses: None. Suggested technical certificates: CompTIA A+, Network +, and Security +.', '977b6b42c59baa02842f5eb0aa092109f5f494b048ec383e8e2138e6299c118d', 21, 21, '21', 198, null, null, false, null),
  ('cb10ea0c-44f1-54fa-8c09-748e7bba3a8f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'ALC Small Group Leader, Drill Sergeant, Detailed Recruiter, Instructor/Writer, WHCA, SFAB, JCU.', 'c903536561cb82095223b2dd355a17484a64b11d0623e4fe5add1950efcc7a32', 21, 21, '21', 199, null, null, false, null),
  ('e8422f05-a119-5c7a-a922-2476c0693ba0', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE', '5db5cbbe6f980b489a8041ba94a06711ad49a1bc8b2aaf832dee11f89f5acc15', 21, 21, '21', 200, null, null, false, null),
  ('2122ecd9-51b1-5cf5-ade2-79aeb1529b03', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'credentials', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Army Credentialing Opportunities', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '33cba142cacd297265afb30b6f7ff9c605a0c57fe0456470d423b7d1bf1a090e', 21, 21, '21', 201, null, null, false, null),
  ('1cbc50c0-a018-5f35-b522-5e86be3ef9fc', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Master Leader Course (MLC). Successful graduation with honors from this course may be a significant promotion factor.', '6d959374d315d399472678204aa6afef406e8cf6a68d858ababb975f643fad4a', 21, 21, '21', 202, null, null, false, null),
  ('27fa25e7-25f7-5260-aa0c-5e361e03435a', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'During this phase of a career, focus should be in tactical assignments as a Platoon Sergeant, Section Chief, Detachment Sergeant, and Senior Signal Operations NCO. The Platoon Sergeant or Section Chief’s job as the senior trainer in the platoon is essential in the development of junior leaders. This experience is also necessary to be competitive for promotion to MSG and appointment to First Sergeant.', '2edca90d5a64fced8c303479742f226156567e39420848a1a6331509343b002f', 21, 21, '21', 203, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec7c1323-23bc-5754-ba7d-37ba82865106', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'DLC 4 completion is a prerequisite of attending MLC. Human Resources Command’s Military Schools Branch (MSB) schedules SFCs for MLC attendance based on Order of Merit. SFCs who have completed all MLC requirements, will automatically be enrolled in DLC 5. Under guided self-development, NCOs and their chain of command must exploit every education opportunity when the OPTEMPO of tactical assignments limit the opportunity for civilian education. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion, but it may be a significant factor and should be pursued whenever possible. A SFC should strive to complete an associate degree prior to eligibility for the Sergeant First Class Evaluation Board. Soldiers should visit the Army IgnitED website for civilian credentials associated with their respective MOS. Upon selection for promotion to Master Sergeant, Sergeants First Class must attend Master Leader Course to be promoted under the Select, Train, Educate, and Promote (STEP) program. There is no DLC requirement for promotion due to the requirement for DLC 4 completion to be eligible for selection to Master Sergeant.', 'dceb6cece119ce08c7739e1e3324660b85c30dd5cd7ada1f0d0209c96c337fd8', 21, 21, '21', 204, null, null, false, null),
  ('da2544cf-e523-529a-b814-86c8ee93e541', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Airborne, Air Assault, and BSNCOC, Signal Digital Master Gunner Course. Suggested certificates: CompTIA A+, Network +, and Security +.', '4414fd10a06c04a73416e355818d27674ba9f52ec38698616de5e00872d18fdc', 21, 21, '21', 205, null, null, false, null),
  ('46c33db4-0c6f-5258-a463-d832a06282d6', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Special assignments', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'Senior Drill Sergeant, Detailed Recruiter, EOA, Observer/Controller, Instructor/Writer, SARC/VA,JCU, DISA, WHCA, TWI, SFAB, Career Management NCO, Career Advisor, West Point Tactical NCO and SLC Small Group Leader.', 'ddd043b936e6a546934ea0a30d836db57f8907fae15614dd919f7bdc035a3edf', 21, 21, '21', 206, null, null, false, null),
  ('4a0057da-67d2-520d-8360-998d0f7c01a8', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25U', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 19. Military Occupational Specialty 25U Signal Operations Support Specialist', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE Army Credentialing Opportunities. Credentialing opportunities are available at the Army IgnitED website located at https://www.armyignited.com.', '6833df983a1c7651bf513eb68c289ab5c28f3b8a04b8781a7c069c0a2d12b29d', 21, 21, '21', 207, null, null, false, null),
  ('ea2efe08-f953-5c1c-835a-7eca90f53dc2', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'The purpose of the Career Progression Plan is to inform Soldiers the Signal Corps’ intent for career pattern, talent management, and professional development. NCOs should steadily increase their technical and basic Soldiering attributes. NCOs should use online training resources to continue to develop and enhance the skills needed to support the modular force. To maintain signal proficiency as professional Senior NCOs, their assignments must focus on challenging and demanding jobs such as First Sergeant, Senior Enlisted Advisor, Chief Signal NCO (Battalion or higher echelon), Corps Signal NCO, and Senior Enlisted Leader. Follow-on staff assignments will add to their overall professional knowledge. MSGs and SGMs/CSMs should ensure assignment diversity throughout their career path.', '261601f53ad0c74ff9c1a50d24620a2d1d6087886b3f3ba52bbfdebe838027dd', 22, 22, '22', 208, null, null, false, null),
  ('2891a713-8284-554b-98cb-dbef07457456', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'The critical assignment for a Master Sergeant is First Sergeant. Time served in a First Sergeant position could prove pivotal towards the opportunity for promotion to SGM. It is beneficial for career development to serve as a First Sergeant for a minimum of 18 months (which may consist of one or more assignments). Master Sergeants should have built a well-rounded career path in both strategic and tactical units as well as obtained experience from generating and broadening assignments.', 'fdfc5eba5624c32f5017160f0ee4fa5bed8a4632c4b511034d83e709b5ea100c', 22, 22, '22', 209, null, null, false, null),
  ('1fed58f1-37b9-5b41-a2a0-62f63a44d0e8', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'Under DLC, Master Sergeants will be automatically enrolled in DLC 5 upon selection for the Sergeants Major Academy. DLC 5 tasks are primarily focused at nominative and joint staff levels. MSGs should visit the Army IgnitED website (https://www.armyignited.com) for civilian credentialing associated with their respective MOS. Civilian certifications within IAT/IAM roles are beneficial in enhancing technical proficiency. MSGs should complete a bachelor’s degree while working towards a master’s degree. A college degree is not a requirement for promotion but may be a significant factor for selection to SGM and should be pursued whenever possible.', 'cb2815e4b6b2532587d979b4194d066c5d3002d86d188670903f4d4b0c335be9', 22, 22, '22', 210, null, null, false, null),
  ('6396a591-f8ec-5e68-a8dd-2edd1f52ae48', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'Airborne, Air Assault, Jumpmaster, BSNCOC, Senior Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (SEJPME) Course II, Mission Command Digital Master Gunner Course, Joint C4 Planner Course, Signal Digital Master Gunner Course, Capabilities Development Course, Operational Contract Support Course (OCS), SHARP Foundations Course, Master Resilience Trainer, Master Fitness Trainer, and Company Commander & First Sergeant Pre-Command Course (CCFSPCC).', '4dd345e96a4584422d3eb859d2a08e33ac475141933a7fc018f5e666d4a94f37', 22, 22, '22', 211, null, null, false, null),
  ('06ffdbb3-c315-542e-83c5-6d3942585ec8', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'Senior Talent Management NCO, Senior Career Management NCO, Deputy Commandant NCOA, Branch Chief/1SG NCOA, Chief/Senior Instructor Writer, Chief Training Developer, Military Equal Opportunity Advisor (MEO Advisor), Inspector General, and WHCA.', '17f35fe86c06edbfe1913593640f45ce9ac0a0ba423ce29087d6a325577bbbf8', 22, 22, '22', 212, null, null, false, null),
  ('9b7cde38-7670-5f94-bf17-61c099482b8f', '73a04793-d1ec-5876-bdfb-c7f224470555', 'Army', 'enlisted', '25Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant — Army Career Degree', 'Chapter 22. Military Occupational Specialty 25Z Senior Signal Sergeant', 'See TADECIDE https://www.dodmou.com/TADECIDE.
